le in case my initial pattern recognition was a coincidence. Maybe using mathematical induction or solving the recurrence relation directly.\n\nFirst, the recurrence relation given is f(x + 1) - f(x) = 2x + 3. This is a linear difference equation. The general solution to such equations can be found by finding the homogeneous solution and a particular solution.\n\nThe homogeneous equation is f(x + 1) - f(x) = 0, which has solutions of the form f_h(x) = C, where C is a constant.\n\nNow, find a particular solution f_p(x). Since the nonhomogeneous term is 2x + 3, which is a linear polynomial, we can assume a particular solution of the form f_p(x) = ax\u00b2 + bx + c.\n\nCompute f_p(x + 1) - f_p(x) = a(x + 1)\u00b2 + b(x + 1) + c - [ax\u00b2 + bx + c] = a(x\u00b2 + 2x + 1) + b(x + 1) + c - ax\u00b2 - bx - c = a(2x + 1) + b.\n\nSimplify: 2a x + a + b.\n\nThis should equal 2x + 3. Therefore, we can set up equations:\n\n2a = 2 => a = 1.\n\na + b = 3 => 1 + b = 3 => b = 2.\n\nSo the particular solution is f_p(x) = x\u00b2 + 2x + c. Wait, but the constant term c cancels out in the difference f_p(x + 1) - f_p(x). Therefore, c can be any constant. However, since the homogeneous solution is a constant, we can combine them.\n\nThus, the general solution is f(x) = f_h(x) + f_p(x) = C + x\u00b2 + 2x.\n\nBut wait, combining constants, since f_p(x) = x\u00b2 + 2x + c and f_h(x) = C, the total solution is f(x) = x\u00b2 + 2x + (C + c). Let's denote D = C + c, so f(x) = x\u00b2 + 2x + D.\n\nNow apply the initial condition f(0) = 1. When x = 0, f(0) = 0 + 0 + D = D = 1. Therefore, D = 1.\n\nThus, the general solution is f(x) = x\u00b2 + 2x + 1 = (x + 1)\u00b2, which matches the earlier pattern recognition. So this confirms the formula is correct.\n\nTherefore, f(2012) = (2012 + 1)\u00b2 = 2013\u00b2 = 4,052,169. So both methods lead to the same conclusion, which gives me confidence that this is the correct answer.\n\nAnother way to think about this is using telescoping sums. Since each 